(Page 11 of 49 - 04 - Agent Tools & Interoperability) Tj T*
(Agent Tools & Interoperability) Tj T*
(May 2026) Tj T*
(11) Tj T*
(Discovery) Tj T*
(Vibe coders do not write custom connectors; they locate pre-built MCP servers from three) Tj T*
(primary sources:) Tj T*
(* Public MCP Registries: Publicly available registries host hundreds of pre-built servers) Tj T*
(\(e.g., registry.modelcontextprotocol.io, github.com/mcp\). These are excellent for rapid) Tj T*
(local prototyping but are unvetted and used at your own risk.) Tj T*
(* Third-Party \(3P\) Remote MCP Servers: Vetted platforms expose hosted endpoints.) Tj T*
(Discover managed pre-vetted MCP servers from official sources. For instance, official) Tj T*
(Google-published MCP servers \(e.g., Google Maps, BigQuery, Google Docs\) let your agent) Tj T*
(securely interact with managed services.) Tj T*
(* Internal Registries: Inside an organization, internal tools are exposed as MCP servers and) Tj T*
(cataloged in a secure registry. The technical implementation of this registry is typically) Tj T*
(managed via an API gateway, GCP Agent Registry, or a private microservice portal.) Tj T*
(Applied Tip:) Tj T*
(When making a decision always consider security as a first priority, look for official) Tj T*
(instructions where possible.) Tj T*
(If using public community servers do not pass credentials, consider using services like) Tj T*
(Model Armor to avoid security issues.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
