(Page 15 of 49 - 04 - Agent Tools & Interoperability) Tj T*
(Agent Tools & Interoperability) Tj T*
(May 2026) Tj T*
(15) Tj T*
(Debugging Issues with MCP Servers) Tj T*
(When your agent hallucinates parameters, calls the wrong tool, or fails to parse a) Tj T*
(payload, don't waste time blindly modifying your system instructions. Debug the transport) Tj T*
(pipes directly:) Tj T*
(* MCP Inspector: A native developer tool that runs a local web panel. It lets you manually) Tj T*
(query any local or remote MCP server, view the active tool schemas, manually test) Tj T*
(payload inputs, and inspect the raw JSON-RPC 2.0 packets without initiating your main) Tj T*
(agent workflow.) Tj T*
(* Chrome DevTools: Perfect when running web-based development environments or) Tj T*
(debugging SSE connections, allowing you to trace incoming web streams and check for) Tj T*
(server latencies.) Tj T*
(Vibe Coder Toolkit: Best Practices for MCP Consumption) Tj T*
(To maintain speed without sacrificing stability, vibe coders should adhere to the following) Tj T*
(guidelines when consuming MCP servers:) Tj T*
(Do's \(Best Practices\)) Tj T*
(* Do audit public servers before connection: Always review the code of publicly available,) Tj T*
(open-source MCP servers before attaching them to an agent that has access to your local) Tj T*
(file system or credentials.) Tj T*
(* Do use RAG for tools: Keep your agent's context window clean. Dynamically load tools) Tj T*
(from a registry only when needed, and drop them from context when the task is complete) Tj T*
(to prevent attention dilution.) Tj T*
(?) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
