(Page 16 of 49 - 04 - Agent Tools & Interoperability) Tj T*
(Agent Tools & Interoperability) Tj T*
(May 2026) Tj T*
(16) Tj T*
(* Do leverage internal API Gateways and registries: If possible, rely on internal tool) Tj T*
(registries. This ensures you are consuming approved, governed data schemas rather than) Tj T*
(reinventing the wheel or running unvetted code.) Tj T*
(* Do use the MCP Inspector: When an agent hallucinates a tool call with their arguments,) Tj T*
(use the MCP Inspector or Chrome DevTools to look at the raw transport data rather than) Tj T*
(blindly tweaking the agent's system prompt.) Tj T*
(* Do include HITL: Show tool inputs to the user before calling the server, to avoid malicious) Tj T*
(or accidental data exfiltration) Tj T*
(* Do auditing needs: Log tool usage for audit purposes) Tj T*
(Don'ts \(Common Pitfalls\)) Tj T*
(* Don't build if you can consume: Resist the urge to write custom REST API wrappers.) Tj T*
(Search for an existing MCP server first to maintain the "universal outlet" philosophy.) Tj T*
(* Don't use public, unverified MCPs in production: Open-source MCP servers are fantastic) Tj T*
(for weekend prototypes, but they carry security and reliability risks. Do not tie core) Tj T*
(business logic to unverified public endpoints or API wrapper code.) Tj T*
(* Don't hardcode credentials: During the Configuration phase, never paste API keys or auth) Tj T*
(tokens directly into your agent's prompt or local scripts. Rely on environment variables to) Tj T*
(pass credentials to the MCP server.) Tj T*
(* Don't connect to production: Use the MCP server with a development project, not) Tj T*
(production. LLMs are great at helping design and test applications, so leverage them in a) Tj T*
(safe environment without exposing real data. Be sure that your development environment) Tj T*
(contains non-production data \(or obfuscated data\).) Tj T*
(* Don't use it for updates: If you must connect to real data, set the server to read-only) Tj T*
(mode, which executes all queries as a read-only.) Tj T*
(?) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
