(Page 17 of 49 - 04 - Agent Tools & Interoperability) Tj T*
(Agent Tools & Interoperability) Tj T*
(May 2026) Tj T*
(17) Tj T*
(* Don't provide wide access to all the Projects: Scope your MCP server to a specific project,) Tj T*
(limiting access to only that project's resources where necessary and possible.) Tj T*
(Now we have learnt how to enable vibecoders to leverage the MCP tools for their AI Agent) Tj T*
(building, but AI agent building goes beyond tools, it is to enable users to bring interoperability) Tj T*
(across the ecosystem of applications. We will review how Agent interoperability works in the) Tj T*
(next section.) Tj T*
(Agent-to-Agent \(A2A\) Interoperability) Tj T*
(As AI systems transition into distributed networks of specialized domain experts,) Tj T*
(standardized communication becomes essential for scaling. This section explores the Agent-) Tj T*
(to-Agent \(A2A\) protocol as the foundational layer that resolves ecosystem fragmentation,) Tj T*
(enabling developers to discover, orchestrate, and monetize a globally interoperable) Tj T*
(virtual workforce.) Tj T*
(The Evolution of Agentic Architectures) Tj T*
(To understand where Vibe Coding fits into the evolution of agentic architectures, we can) Tj T*
(observe a recurring pattern in technology: the shift from manual, low-level configuration) Tj T*
(to high-level, intent-based, declarative orchestration when users don't say HOW to build) Tj T*
(something but WHAT they need.) Tj T*
ET
