(Page 18 of 49 - 04 - Agent Tools & Interoperability) Tj T*
(Agent Tools & Interoperability) Tj T*
(May 2026) Tj T*
(18) Tj T*
(A parallel trend is found in the history of IT infrastructure where we transitioned from manual) Tj T*
(configurations to "Infrastructure as Code"  declarative scripts. A similar trend happened) Tj T*
(in the history of Machine Learning. The visionary premise from Google behind Automated) Tj T*
(Machine Learning \(AutoML\) was to democratize AI by automating the "drudge work" of) Tj T*
(model creation:) Tj T*
("One way we hope to make AI more accessible is by simplifying the creation of machine) Tj T*
(learning models called neural networks. Today, designing neural nets is extremely time) Tj T*
(intensive... That's why we've created an approach called AutoML, showing that it's) Tj T*
(possible for neural nets to design neural nets. We hope AutoML will take an ability that a) Tj T*
(few PhDs have today ?." 1) Tj T*
(Today, technology enables us to vibe code entire applications. However, the trajectory) Tj T*
(of agentic architectures used to vibe code these applications is currently mirroring) Tj T*
(one of the most significant shifts in software history: the transition from Monolithic to) Tj T*
(Microservices architectures.) Tj T*
(Just as early web applications were built as single, massive codebases where every function) Tj T*
(\(billing, UI, database\) was tightly coupled, many initial vibe coding projects relied on a "Swiss) Tj T*
(Army knife" Single Agent Monolith. This involves relying on a single, highly sophisticated) Tj T*
(prompt where one agent wears multiple hats with many connected tools to handle everything) Tj T*
(from database queries to UI rendering and testing. While this allows a developer to wire) Tj T*
(together a prototype in a weekend, it eventually hits the same "Monolithic Ceiling" that) Tj T*
(plagued early web apps:) Tj T*
(* Scaling Friction: You cannot optimize just the "Database logic" without potentially) Tj T*
(confusing the "UI logic" residing in the same prompt. Also, the more tools a single agent) Tj T*
(has access to, the worse its decision-making becomes. The search space for its next) Tj T*
(action is simply too large, leading to hallucinated parameters or triggering the wrong tools.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
