(Page 19 of 49 - 04 - Agent Tools & Interoperability) Tj T*
(Agent Tools & Interoperability) Tj T*
(May 2026) Tj T*
(19) Tj T*
(* Contextual Overload: Shoving overarching system instructions, dozens of complex tool) Tj T*
(schemas, and ongoing conversation history into a single prompt quickly maxes out the) Tj T*
(model's working memory.) Tj T*
(* The Single Point of Failure: A bug in one "tool" or instruction can cause the entire agent) Tj T*
(to hallucinate or crash. Irrelevant or corrupted data stored in context gets carried over,) Tj T*
(breaking future reasoning.) Tj T*
(To overcome these bottlenecks one can follow a similar blueprint laid out by ML engineers) Tj T*
(and software engineers years ago. When early AutoML models successfully proved their) Tj T*
(business value, teams rarely left those auto-generated black boxes running the core) Tj T*
(business. To reach production scale they had to break this black box apart into observable,) Tj T*
(maintainable stages--data versioning, feature stores, drift detection. By specializing) Tj T*
(the components they applied a fundamental law of system design: specialization as a) Tj T*
(scaling mechanism.) Tj T*
(Figure 3: Monolithic Multi-agent Architecture) Tj T*
ET
