(Page 20 of 49 - 04 - Agent Tools & Interoperability) Tj T*
(Agent Tools & Interoperability) Tj T*
(May 2026) Tj T*
(20) Tj T*
(Internal specialization works by logically partitioning a monolithic agent into distinct,) Tj T*
(purpose-built sub-agents. Each agent is governed by a highly focused system prompt) Tj T*
(and a relevant subset of tools. It is still monolith because these internal sub-agents do) Tj T*
(not communicate across network boundaries. Instead, they share the same runtime and) Tj T*
(underlying memory.) Tj T*
(This logical partitioning allows developers to modularize complex definitions while) Tj T*
(maintaining the low-latency execution and simplified state management inherent to a single-) Tj T*
(process application. At the same time this modularity addresses the inherent limitations of) Tj T*
(single-agent systems through several key technical improvements:) Tj T*
(* Reduction of Search Space: By restricting a sub-agent's tools and skills \(e.g., giving a DB) Tj T*
(agent only query tools\), we drastically reduce tool-call errors and hallucinations.) Tj T*
(* Mitigation of Attention Dilution: Specialization allows the underlying LLM to focus on a) Tj T*
(single domain prompt, leading to sharper reasoning.) Tj T*
(* Optimization of Contextual Load: Because the orchestrator routes tasks instead of) Tj T*
(processing the entire logic tree, sub-agents maintain a high signal-to-noise ratio in their) Tj T*
(context windows.) Tj T*
(As agentic architectures mature, a significant ecosystem shift based on distributed) Tj T*
(multi-agent architectures is underway. Industry leaders--including Google, Salesforce,) Tj T*
(ServiceNow, and Workday--are moving beyond the provision of APIs. These organizations are) Tj T*
(deploying domain-specific AI agents designed to navigate their proprietary ecosystems with) Tj T*
(native precision.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
