(Page 21 of 49 - 04 - Agent Tools & Interoperability) Tj T*
(Agent Tools & Interoperability) Tj T*
(May 2026) Tj T*
(21) Tj T*
(Figure 4: Distributed Multi-Agent Architecture. An orchestrator delegates tasks across network boundaries) Tj T*
(to remote, domain-specific agents.) Tj T*
(This shift presents a strategic opportunity for developers. However, to reach the next tier of) Tj T*
(scale, technical and business leaders must ruthlessly prioritize their focus through a modern) Tj T*
("Build vs. Buy" lens.) Tj T*
(While it is technically feasible to construct a multi-agent system using custom-built sub-) Tj T*
(agents for third-party platforms \(e.g. custom subagent for ServiceNow or custom subagent) Tj T*
(for Salesforce etc\), this approach introduces a significant Maintenance Tax. By opting for) Tj T*
(bespoke development of domain specialists, the developer assumes full responsibility for) Tj T*
(updating prompt logic and tool definitions reflecting upstream product updates and API) Tj T*
(schema changes.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
