(May 2026) Tj T*
(24) Tj T*
(yAn agent, however, operates in an unbounded problem-solving space. Real-world software) Tj T*
(environments are full of ambiguous data structures, misleading requirements, and conflicting) Tj T*
(user preferences. You rarely can specify all necessary details in a complex workflow without) Tj T*
(multi-turn clarification. The digital equivalent of crooked walls.) Tj T*
(The GOTO Problem in Agentic Architecture) Tj T*
(Because an agent's domain is unbounded, trying to force an agent into a standard tool) Tj T*
(wrapper introduces the architectural equivalent of a GOTO statement into your orchestrator.) Tj T*
(When you call a collaborative agent, the control flow leaves the expected, structured context.) Tj T*
(The agent might hit an interrupted state, request more information, and potentially never) Tj T*
(return the expected output to the original caller if the user changes their mind or abandons) Tj T*
(the prompt.) Tj T*
(You need a paradigm that isolates this messy, multi-turn state. You need a protocol that) Tj T*
(allows the domain agent to pause its execution, reach back out to the Orchestrator, negotiate) Tj T*
(a solution, and then resume its work without losing its conversational state.) Tj T*
(That is exactly the gap the A2A protocol fills. By isolating this collaborative routing to the) Tj T*
(A2A layer, we keep the tool layer \(MCP\) clean, predictable, and strictly structured.) Tj T*
(Building the Virtual Workforce) Tj T*
(The introduction of the A2A protocol and the shift toward specialization does more than just) Tj T*
(solve technical bottlenecks--it creates the foundations for new marketplaces for expertise) Tj T*
(which represents a new model in how value is delivered.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
