(Page 25 of 49 - 04 - Agent Tools & Interoperability) Tj T*
(Agent Tools & Interoperability) Tj T*
(May 2026) Tj T*
(25) Tj T*
(Without A2A, a developer might build an application and struggle to maintain its growing) Tj T*
(complexity. In the A2A era, that same developer can focus on perfecting a high-value niche--) Tj T*
(such as an agent that specializes in "Real-time Regulatory Compliance". Whether built as a) Tj T*
(sophisticated multi-agent monolith or a distributed app, these systems can now be exposed) Tj T*
(to the world as A2A-compliant agents. This means that a specialist vibe coded in one part of) Tj T*
(the world can be discovered and "hired" by another Orchestrator across the globe.) Tj T*
(The Agent Card) Tj T*
(To facilitate this discovery, every agent is defined by an Agent Card. This is the standardized) Tj T*
("CV" of the AI world, providing a machine-readable identity that outlines:) Tj T*
(* Capabilities: What tasks the agent can perform.) Tj T*
(* Security & Compliance: Its data handling policies and permission requirements.) Tj T*
(* Interaction Schemas: How other agents should communicate with it via the A2A protocol.) Tj T*
(Registries: From Public Marketplaces to Private Enterprises) Tj T*
(Once an agent is equipped with its Agent Card, it can be registered within an Agent Registry) Tj T*
(whose goal is to turn Agents into discoverable services. This offers two primary paths) Tj T*
(for developers:) Tj T*
(1. Public Registries \(Marketplaces\): Like a global talent agency, public registries allow) Tj T*
(developers to list their specialist agents for the world to find. This paves the way for) Tj T*
(building specialist agents for a specific industry and licensing its expertise to thousands of) Tj T*
(other orchestrators.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
