(Agent Tools & Interoperability) Tj T*
(May 2026) Tj T*
(26) Tj T*
(2. Private Registries: Within the enterprise, Agent Registries provide a secure, governed) Tj T*
(environment. Developers inside a large corporation can build a specialist agent that) Tj T*
(automates an internal workflow and register it for use by other departments, ensuring that) Tj T*
(expertise is shared across corporate boundaries without compromising security.) Tj T*
(Ultimately, the A2A protocol transforms the act of building isolated agentic applications into) Tj T*
(building the foundational members of a global, interoperable digital workforce.) Tj T*
(Implementing A2A Protocols) Tj T*
(The practical implementation of the A2A architecture enables two distinct) Tj T*
(development motions:) Tj T*
(* exposing AI agent as A2A agent \(the supply side\)) Tj T*
(* orchestrating remote A2A agents \(the demand side\)) Tj T*
(Exposing A2A Agent) Tj T*
(Packaging an agent for the A2A ecosystem involves three core steps:) Tj T*
(* Defining the Agent Card: Formal agent specification.) Tj T*
(* Implementing the Agent Executor \(The Translation Layer\): It translates incoming) Tj T*
(A2A requests and responses into the specific calls required by the underlying agentic) Tj T*
(frameworks \(e.g., ADK, LangGraph, or  bespoke enterprise code\).) Tj T*
(* Establishing the A2A Endpoint: Executor must be exposed as an) Tj T*
(A2A-compliant endpoint.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
