(standardized pattern for agents to securely advertise, negotiate, and execute optional,) Tj T*
(higher-order functionalities that transcend basic message passing.) Tj T*
(Three foundational frameworks that operate as native extensions atop the core A2A) Tj T*
(foundation include the Agent-to-User Interface \(A2UI\), designed to generate dynamic,) Tj T*
(stateful user experiences; the Universal Commerce Protocol \(UCP\), engineered to facilitate) Tj T*
(secure, autonomous agentic commerce; and the Agent Payments Protocol \(AP2\) which) Tj T*
(lays the groundwork for trusted, verifiable agentic payments. All three are discussed in more) Tj T*
(detail in the following sections.) Tj T*
(Monetizing A2A Agents) Tj T*
(Making an agent work is only half the battle; the other half is ensuring long-term commercial) Tj T*
(sustainability. Following the success of the Software-as-a-Service \(SaaS\) paradigm, the A2A) Tj T*
(protocol naturally enables an Agent-as-a-Service \(AaaS\) model. This allows specialized) Tj T*
(agents to be offered in a consumption-based model through various sales channels.) Tj T*
(One example is utilizing the Google Cloud Marketplace as a monetization engine.) Tj T*
(Independent agent/software vendors and developers can list their A2A agents on the) Tj T*
(marketplace to instantly leverage the existing base of Google Cloud enterprise customers.) Tj T*
(Customers can procure these specialists and at the same time utilize their existing GCP) Tj T*
(financial commitments. Win-win for everyone.) Tj T*
(The marketplace infrastructure automatically handles the "hard part"--complex billing--) Tj T*
(by providing native support for hybrid pricing, such as the "Flat fee with usage" model.) Tj T*
(This allows vendors to charge a predictable base fee while monetizing compute or) Tj T*
(token-based overages.) Tj T*
ET
