(Page 32 of 49 - 04 - Agent Tools & Interoperability) Tj T*
(Agent Tools & Interoperability) Tj T*
(May 2026) Tj T*
(32) Tj T*
(Agent-to-UI \(A2UI\) Interoperability) Tj T*
(The Communication Gap) Tj T*
(When you ask a colleague, "How did Q4 perform by region?" they don't hand you a) Tj T*
(spreadsheet. They sketch a bar chart on the whiteboard, circle the standout regions, and add) Tj T*
(context. This is how humans share insights: through visuals and interaction.) Tj T*
(Yet our agents return raw JSON. You then build the chart yourself. Import libraries, configure) Tj T*
(axes, manage state. This context-switching between asking for insights and doing frontend) Tj T*
(work breaks the vibe coding flow.) Tj T*
(Agent-to-UI \(A2UI\) interoperability resolves this enabling Agents to generate complete,) Tj T*
(interactive user interfaces as outputs: not just JSON blobs.) Tj T*
(Generative UI & A2UI) Tj T*
(What is Generative UI?) Tj T*
(Generative UI is the concept of LLMs dynamically creating user interfaces at runtime based) Tj T*
(on user intent and context. Instead of developers hard-coding every possible UI state, the) Tj T*
(model generates appropriate interfaces on demand. When you ask "Compare Q4 sales by) Tj T*
(region", the system doesn't just retrieve data: it composes an interactive layout, cards, filters,) Tj T*
(and controls, tailored to that specific request.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
