(Page 33 of 49 - 04 - Agent Tools & Interoperability) Tj T*
(Agent Tools & Interoperability) Tj T*
(May 2026) Tj T*
(33) Tj T*
(This represents a shift from static, pre-built interfaces to dynamic, context-aware UIs. The) Tj T*
(challenge is doing this safely. Running arbitrary UI code generated by an LLM can pose) Tj T*
(security risks: code injection, XSS attacks, and uncontrolled side effects.) Tj T*
(A2UI: A Secure Implementation) Tj T*
(A2UI is a framework-agnostic standard for declaring UI intent -- Google's open-) Tj T*
(source way of letting agents describe interfaces in a portable, declarative format instead of) Tj T*
(streaming raw data or shipping arbitrary code.) Tj T*
(To see why a format matters here, think about how a composer ships their work. They don't) Tj T*
(hand musicians a recording: they hand them sheet music. The same score plays on a piano,) Tj T*
(an orchestra, or a synthesizer; each instrument interprets the notation through its own voice.) Tj T*
(A2UI is sheet music for UI: the agent writes the intent \(what to render and how it composes\),) Tj T*
(and any renderer \(e.g. React, Angular, Lit, Flutter, Jetpack Compose, SwiftUI, etc\) performs) Tj T*
(it natively on the device the user actually has. The agent doesn't need to know whether) Tj T*
(you're targeting web, mobile, wearable, or appliance, it just knows the catalog of available) Tj T*
(components and any examples you want to give.) Tj T*
(That separation of concerns is what makes A2UI safe. The agent doesn't generate executable) Tj T*
(code \(a security nightmare\) and it doesn't ship pre-rendered pixels \(which can't reflow) Tj T*
(or stay interactive\). Instead it requests components from a trusted catalog \(e.g. buttons,) Tj T*
(text fields, cards, your own charts\) and the client renders them using its own component) Tj T*
(library. The catalog defines what's available, the agent decides how to arrange them, the) Tj T*
(client assembles the final structure. Compositional, like LEGO blocks, but the blocks are UI) Tj T*
(components from your design system.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
