(May 2026) Tj T*
(36) Tj T*
(The default is to let the LLM emit A2UI directly: the model owns the layout, adapts it to user) Tj T*
(intent, and the same agent handles "compare these regions" and "show me trends" with) Tj T*
(different interfaces. Production code for this pattern uses the official a2ui-agent-sdk and) Tj T*
(lives in 4.4.) Tj T*
(The specialization is to have a tool return a fixed A2UI structure: one tool call, no LLM tokens) Tj T*
(spent on UI generation, fully predictable output. This is the right call when the layout is) Tj T*
(deterministic from inputs: every region's sales dashboard looks the same, every booking form) Tj T*
(has the same fields. Effectively, the tool is a server-side template.) Tj T*
(A clean tool-as-template tool does two things in its body: build the A2UI structure with) Tj T*
(data bindings \(path references, not f-string interpolation\) and return it. The framework's) Tj T*
(A2uiPartConverter \(from a2ui-agent-sdk\) intercepts the tool's response and routes it to) Tj T*
(the client as an A2UI part, so the tool itself stays a plain Python function:) Tj T*
(Python) Tj T*
(from google.adk.agents import LlmAgent) Tj T*
(from google.adk.models import Gemini) Tj T*
(def  get_sales_dashboard\(region: str\) -> dict:) Tj T*
("""Build a data-bound sales dashboard for `region`.""") Tj T*
(data = fetch_sales\(region\)) Tj T*
(return {) Tj T*
("version": "v0.9",) Tj T*
("updateComponents": {) Tj T*
("surfaceId": "sales",) Tj T*
("components": [) Tj T*
({"id": "root", "component": "Column",) Tj T*
("children": ["title", "total", "drill"]},) Tj T*
({"id": "title", "component": "Text",) Tj T*
("text": {"path": "/title"}, "variant": "h1"},) Tj T*
(Continues next page...) Tj T*
