(Page 43 of 49 - 04 - Agent Tools & Interoperability) Tj T*
(Agent Tools & Interoperability) Tj T*
(May 2026) Tj T*
(43) Tj T*
(Summary) Tj T*
(Generative UI lets LLMs create user interfaces at runtime based on user intent. A2UI is) Tj T*
(Google's open-source standard for doing this safely: a framework-agnostic format for) Tj T*
(declaring UI intent, so the same agent message renders natively in Lit, Flutter, React, or your) Tj T*
(own design system.) Tj T*
(The security model matters: agents can't inject arbitrary code. They can only request) Tj T*
(components the renderer's catalog already trusts. That's what makes A2UI safe while still) Tj T*
(enabling dynamic, generative interfaces.) Tj T*
(Agents and Commerce \(AP2 and UCP\)) Tj T*
(Autonomous Procurement with a workflow example) Tj T*
(Vibe coders learn checkout, catalog , order capability and mandate with their agents.) Tj T*
(Key characteristics and benefits of Protocols) Tj T*
(Typed schemas, Security and open source \(Integration debt and vendor neutrality\)) Tj T*
(Lab recommendations:) Tj T*
(https://codelabs.developers.google.com/next26/adk-agent-commerce#0) Tj T*
ET
endstream
